# AWS DynamoDB

I help you work with DynamoDB for NoSQL data.

## DynamoDB Client
```typescript
import { DynamoDBClient } from '@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb';
import { DynamoDBDocumentClient, PutCommand, GetCommand, QueryCommand } from '@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb';

const client = new DynamoDBClient({ region: process.env.AWS_REGION });
const docClient = DynamoDBDocumentClient.from(client);
```

## CRUD Operations
```typescript
// Create
await docClient.send(new PutCommand({
  TableName: 'Users',
  Item: { pk: 'USER#123', sk: 'PROFILE', name: 'John', email: 'john@example.com' },
}));

// Read
const result = await docClient.send(new GetCommand({
  TableName: 'Users',
  Key: { pk: 'USER#123', sk: 'PROFILE' },
}));

// Query (all items for a user)
const items = await docClient.send(new QueryCommand({
  TableName: 'Users',
  KeyConditionExpression: 'pk = :pk',
  ExpressionAttributeValues: { ':pk': 'USER#123' },
}));
```

## Single Table Design
```
| pk          | sk           | Data |
|-------------|--------------|------|
| USER#123    | PROFILE      | User info |
| USER#123    | ORDER#001    | Order info |
| USER#123    | ORDER#002    | Order info |
| ORDER#001   | ORDER#001    | Order details |
```

# AWS IAM Security

I help you implement secure IAM policies.

## Least Privilege Policy
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/uploads/*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "dynamodb:GetItem",
        "dynamodb:PutItem",
        "dynamodb:Query"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/MyTable"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Role-Based Access
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "lambda.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Security Best Practices
- Never use root credentials
- Enable MFA for all users
- Use roles instead of access keys
- Apply least privilege principle
- Rotate credentials regularly
- Use AWS Organizations for multi-account
- Enable CloudTrail for auditing
