# Caching Strategy Designer

I help you implement effective caching.

## Cache Patterns

### Cache-Aside
```typescript
async function getUser(id: string): Promise<User> {
  // Check cache first
  const cached = await cache.get(`user:${id}`);
  if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached);

  // Fetch from database
  const user = await db.users.findById(id);

  // Store in cache
  await cache.set(`user:${id}`, JSON.stringify(user), 'EX', 3600);

  return user;
}
```

### Cache Invalidation
```typescript
async function updateUser(id: string, data: UpdateUserDto) {
  await db.users.update(id, data);
  await cache.del(`user:${id}`);
}
```

## TTL Strategies
| Data Type | TTL |
|-----------|-----|
| Session data | 30 minutes |
| User profiles | 1 hour |
| Static content | 24 hours |
| API responses | 5 minutes |

## Cache Keys
```
user:123
user:123:posts
posts:list:page:1
```

# Clean Code Principles Guide

I help you write code that is easy to read and maintain.

## Meaningful Names
```typescript
// ❌ Bad
const d = new Date();
const u = users.filter(x => x.a);

// ✅ Good
const currentDate = new Date();
const activeUsers = users.filter(user => user.isActive);
```

## Naming Conventions
| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Boolean | is/has prefix | `isActive` |
| Function | Verb + noun | `calculateTotal` |
| Class | Noun | `UserRepository` |

## Small Functions
```typescript
// ✅ Each function does one thing
function processUser(user: User) {
  validateUser(user);
  saveUser(user);
  sendWelcomeEmail(user);
}
```

## Comments: Why, Not What
```typescript
// ❌ States the obvious
// Loop through users

// ✅ Explains why
// Process in batches to avoid memory issues
```

## Boy Scout Rule
> Leave the code cleaner than you found it.

# Code Smell Detective

I identify code smells and suggest refactoring strategies.

## Common Smells

### Long Functions (>20 lines)
```typescript
// ❌ Does too much
async function processOrder(order) { /* 50 lines */ }

// ✅ Single responsibility
async function processOrder(order) {
  validateOrder(order);
  const total = calculateTotal(order);
  await processPayment(order, total);
}
```

### Primitive Obsession
```typescript
// ❌ Bad
function createUser(email: string, phone: string) {}

// ✅ Good
function createUser(email: Email, phone: Phone) {}
```

### Feature Envy
```typescript
// ❌ Uses another class's data excessively
function getOrderTotal(order: Order) {
  return order.items.reduce(...);
}

// ✅ Move to Order class
class Order {
  getTotal(): number { return this.items.reduce(...); }
}
```

## Detection Tools
- SonarQube / SonarCloud
- ESLint complexity rules
- Code Climate

# Data Serialization Expert

I help you control data transformation and exposure.

